WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:12.469
Alcohol has been with us since 10,000 BC,
the ancient Egyptians had 17 types of beer

00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:14.250
and 24 variates of wine.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:18.170
In fact, beer was a dietary staple long before
bread.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.360
But what exactly is alcohol?

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.690
Alcohol what we call a special group of chemicals.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:26.220
Ethanol is the only drinkable alcohol.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.940
Ethanol is what you drink on a friday night.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:35.059
But other types of alcohol include methanol
and isopropanol, however I would highly recommend

00:00:35.059 --> 00:00:40.079
against drinking these, they are used in many
different fields, including medical.

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:44.620
The human body constantly produces small amounts
of alcohol itself.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:48.290
Alcohol is a drug, a depressant to be precise.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:53.280
However in small doses it can act as a stimulant,
it's only when you consume too much that it's

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:58.200
depressant effects kick in and you end up
feeling like this.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:04.019
Alcohol slows down your vital functions, causing
slurred speech, unsteady movement, an ability

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:07.409
to react quickly and generally bad decisions.

00:01:07.409 --> 00:01:11.390
But why do we get a hangover when we drink
too much?

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:16.430
Well hangovers are pretty damn nasty, but
what do you expect, alcohol is essentially

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:17.430
a poison.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:23.049
I'm sure you're already well aware but let
me remind you of the symptoms of a hangover:

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.560
Dehydration
Dry mouth

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.140
Tiredness
Headache

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:27.759
Nausea
Weakness

00:01:27.759 --> 00:01:29.729
Anxiety
Irritability

00:01:29.729 --> 00:01:32.049
Pessimism
Reduced concentration

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:35.329
Sensitivity to light and noise
Trouble sleeping

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:38.799
And a general feeling of "talk to me and you'll
regret it"

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:42.829
But what is it about alcohol that causes these
symptoms.

00:01:42.829 --> 00:01:47.899
The biggest factor is dehydration, alcohol
is a diuretic, this means you pee more and

00:01:47.899 --> 00:01:50.039
dehydrate very fast.

00:01:50.039 --> 00:01:55.359
This is exactly the reason you get a headache,
whilst dehydrated your body takes water from

00:01:55.359 --> 00:02:00.770
the brain to give to other parts of your body,
causing your brain to literally shrink and

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:03.020
that can be very painful.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:07.689
Alcohol is produced through the process of
fermentation, were various foods are fermented

00:02:07.689 --> 00:02:12.030
with yeast, during this process the yeast
converts malt sugars into alcohol.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:16.530
Beer is made of 4 basic ingredients: Barley,
water, hops and yeast.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.720
But the process of wine making is a bit more
complicated.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:25.240
Firstly the grapes are picked and hand sorted
to remove things like sticks and rocks.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.900
The grapes are then crushed and destemmed.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:31.130
They are then mixed with yeast, various nutrients
and acid.

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:35.540
The mixture is then fermented for a couple
of weeks, a device called a hydrometer is

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:41.420
used to measure the alcohol vs sugar levels
and determine when the wine is just right.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:45.490
The mixture is then put into a big press and,
you guessed it, pressed.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:47.300
The resulting liquid is collected.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:52.370
Oak chips are added for flavour and the wine
is left to sit for months and months.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:57.620
During this time the wine is transferred from
bottle to bottle until the liquid is completely

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:58.620
clear.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:03.270
Campden tablets are then added, this kills
bacteria and stops any further fermentation.

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:08.590
The wine is then bottled, sealed with a cork
or screw top and left to age for years until

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:09.720
it is finally consumed.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:15.460
If a wine has "corked", it has reacted with
the cork and spoiled inside the bottle.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:20.350
The world's biggest consumer of alcohol, per
person, is the Czech Republic, drinking an

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:25.110
astonishing 15 litres of alcohol per person,
per year.

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:30.360
In fact as a continent Europe is by far the
world's biggest alcohol consumer.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:34.300
The top 13 countries for getting pissed are
all European.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:41.000
Shamefully the United Kingdom is only 15th
on the list, guzzling down 11.7 litres of

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.700
alcohol per person, every year.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:48.070
Way ahead of the United States at only 8.5
litres per person.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:53.160
In most countries the legal drinking age is
18, only 12 countries have a drinking age

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:58.410
above 18 and there are 19 countries where
there is absolutely no legal drinking age

00:03:58.410 --> 00:03:59.880
at all.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:05.731
Internationally, the average age when a person
first tastes an alcoholic beverage is 12 and

00:04:05.731 --> 00:04:11.270
shockingly more than 80% of people are regular
drinkers by age 15.

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:16.510
In small amounts alcohol can have health benefits
on your heart, although there are countless

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:20.670
harmful effects on the body when drunk regularly
in large quantities.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:25.370
But alcohol is fun and can leave you with
many good memories or none at all.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:27.419
So go out and enjoy yourself!

00:04:27.419 --> 00:04:54.259
Just don't overdo it.

